To create search_flights.py in AITesting directory using Playwright MCP, following prompt was used:

Generate and execute a Playwright test framework suite to automate purchase from a retail website using pytest and Playwright MCP.

Test Scenario:

Launch URL: https://www.saucedemo.com
Login with username: standard_user and password: secret_sauce
Add all items >$10 to the cart.
Proceed to checkout and complete the purchase.
Fetch order details and save them to a file named order_details.txt.

Implementation Requirements:

Use pytest style structure (functions starting with test_).
Execute each step interactively through Playwright MCP tools.
Once all steps are succeeded, generate and save the final test framework folder inside 'PlaywrightAutomationFramework' directory.
Run the saved test automatically in headed mode (browser should be visible).
In any step, if any step or assertion got failed, identify and fix the issue then rerun until the test passes.

Expected Output:

A fully working Playwright automation framework in python having following structure:
 playwright-framework/
├── tests/                  # Test scripts (pytest files)
│   ├── conftest.py         # Fixtures and setup/teardown
│   ├── test_login.py
│   └── test_dashboard.py
├── pages/                  # Page Object Models (Locators & Actions)
│   ├── base_page.py
│   ├── login_page.py
│   └── dashboard_page.py
├── data/                   # Test data (JSON, CSV, or YAML)
│   └── user_data.json
├── utils/                  # Helper functions (API, DB, Logging)
│   └── config_reader.py
├── reports/                # Test execution reports and screenshots
├── pytest.ini              # Pytest configuration
├── requirements.txt        # Dependencies
└── .env                    # Environment variables (Secrets)
The script should automate the complete flow described above and successfully return the order details.